Absolutely. Your Production Support Console can become much more than a dashboard that displays whether feeds and jobs are running.

I would design it as an end-to-end Production Operations & Intelligent Diagnostics Platform. An engineer should be able to select Application A, understand its entire processing flow, identify exactly where a failure occurred, trace the dependent jobs and feeds, collect evidence, and prepare a troubleshooting report—all from the same desktop UI.

The key is to move through four levels:
1. Monitor — What is happening?
2. Diagnose — Why is it happening?
3. Investigate — What is the impact, and what evidence supports the issue?
4. Resolve — What approved action can be taken to fix it?
Here are the advanced features I would consider implementing.
1. Application dependency map — visualize the entire processing flow
Instead of showing only tables, create a visual dependency map for every application.

For example, selecting Application A could display:
