6. Production incident correlation
This is where the platform becomes significantly more powerful.

Imagine three problems appear around the same time:
- An invoice feed is delayed.
- An AutoSys job fails.
- A TWS job remains waiting.
Instead of presenting three unrelated alerts, the application groups them into a single potential incident.

Incident: Application A processing delay
Evidence	Status
Invoice feed	Delayed
AutoSys predecessor	Failed
TWS downstream job	Waiting
Database connectivity	Healthy
Application service	Healthy


The system can then suggest:
The delayed invoice feed and failed AutoSys job may be related. Investigate the failed predecessor and verify the expected input file before considering a rerun.

The application should distinguish confirmed dependencies from possible correlations. This avoids incorrectly attributing a failure to an unrelated event.
